 ## Overview
-A U-Net based denoiser is a convolutional neural network used to enhance reconstructed volumes or images by removing noise and artifacts [S1, unofficial]. It operates as a post-processing step, taking a noisy input and auxiliary features to predict a clean output [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from kernel-prediction methods by using a fixed encoder-decoder architecture with skip connections rather than predicting spatially varying kernels [S1, 13214-spatiotemporal-kernel-prediction-network-for-vpt.md, unofficial].
+A U-Net based denoiser is a convolutional neural network used to enhance reconstructed volumes or images by removing noise and artifacts [S1, unofficial]. It operates as a post-processing step, taking a noisy input to predict a clean output [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from kernel-prediction methods by using a fixed encoder-decoder architecture rather than predicting spatially varying kernels [G]. It builds on the shared principles of neural auxiliary feature denoising [Parent](10536-denoising-via-neural-auxiliary-features.md).
 
 ## How it works
 **Inputs and Outputs:**
